I had a similar idea a few days ago during a particularly boring
session of biodiversity reduction.

I was thinking of Angband, and came to the conclusion that
Angband-like unique monsters would not add much to Nethack, due to the
lack of diversity.  Uniques in Angband fall into one of two camps -
those that either come with or can summon a huge horde of minions, and
those which are extremely fast.  Defeating the first type involves
either fighting in a corridor or (in extreme cases) building an
anti-summoning corridor.  Defeating the second type is nearly
impossible until you have found those +5 speed boots or ring of speed.

However, the idea as described here is subtly different - the uniques
will not necessarily be hostile, they will not necessarily be
accompanied by a horde of nasties, they will have interesting stories,
and some (like Wendy) will have a guaranteed useful early-ish item.  I
think that with these tweaks the addition of unique monsters would add
a huge amout of variety, and most importantly fun, to the game.

